source: crates/instrukt-cli/tests/roles-and-capabilities.rs
expression: h.help()
---
Context engineering for coding agents

Usage: instrukt <COMMAND>

Commands:
  status     Read computer/repository setup, adoption and publication before changing instrukt
  bugs       Park, inspect and remove known-issue dispositions for the log bug hunter
  discuss    Open or close this native thread's conversation link
  agents     Configured profiles and expiring profile/model availability
  secrets    Store or generate protected machine-local secrets
  config     Read, edit, initialize and validate `instrukt.yaml`
  docs       Validate, list and read documentation snippets
  sync       Publish the current project's committed docs into the home
  init       Adopt instrukt in the current git repository
  hooks      Install, remove, inspect and run instrukt's git hook sections
  repo       Attributed commits in an authoring worktree
  specs      Use-case coverage, reservation and trace
  blueprint  Structural graph queries (blueprint module)
  todo       The work record and workflow (todos module)
  eval       Evaluation reports from the work record
  events     Discover producer-declared event types and their schemas
  history    Extract, import and search retained conversations across computers
  webhooks   Internal signed loopback webhook receiver (installation is separate)
  run        Run the runner until stopped
  tick       One runner wake-up, as the OS scheduler invokes it
  ticks      Scheduled tick status
  sessions   Inspect keyed runtime threads and resolve uncertain unattended starts
  install    Converge/check module infrastructure across adopted projects; repair with the same
             command
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help     Print help
  -V, --version  Print version

Role: builder · class: agent. Scope comes from assignment
instrukt:standing:reactions%2Fprocedure%2Frespond@project%3Afork. Object claims, phase and writer
constraints apply.
Usual capabilities: role: builder; class: agent; grants: docs-read:any, docs-write:own,
todo-read:any, todo-write:own, artifact-read:any, artifact-write:own, stamp:own, agents-read:any,
config-read:any, repository-read:any, code-commit:own, code-check:any, eval-read:any,
events-read:any, installation-read:any
